# Vulnerabilities intentionally accepted after review.
# Each entry MUST have a comment explaining why - never ignore silently.
#
# npm's own bundled internal CLI tooling (usr/local/lib/node_modules/npm/...)
# is excluded from scanning entirely via `skip-dirs` in the CI workflow,
# since it ships inside the Node.js base image and our app never invokes
# or exposes it at runtime - it is not part of our real dependency tree
# or attack surface (our own dependencies live under /app/node_modules,
# which only contains express and morgan).

# libssl3 / libcrypto3 (Alpine base image OpenSSL libraries) - fix is
# released upstream (3.5.7-r0) but hasn't landed in the currently
# published node:20-alpine tag yet. Our app does not call
# PKCS7_verify() or otherwise process untrusted PKCS7 data, so this
# specific vulnerability has no practical exploit path here. Re-check
# at each Dockerfile base image bump.
CVE-2026-45447
